\maketitle

\begin{abstract}
We present the final Alpha iteration of L-ToEC, resolving the "Infinite Regress" of the substrate through the principle of Ouroboric Closure. We argue that the universe is not a linear stack but a self-referential strange loop where the Substrate ($\substrate$) and the Interface ($\interface$) co-constitute one another. The "Hardware" is the extensional manifestation of the "Logic," and the "Logic" is the intensional manifestation of the "Hardware."
\end{abstract}

\section{The Ouroboric Closure}
The Critic's "Death Blow" assumes a linear causality where a substrate must be "run" by a prior medium. We reject this linear topology in favor of a circular one.

\begin{axiom}[Ouroboric Grounding]
The Substrate ($\leech$) is the "Information Potential" of the system, while the Interface ($\interface$) is the "Information Realization." The system is a self-executing strange loop:
\begin{equation}
\substrate \xrightarrow{Protocol} \interface \xrightarrow{Observation} \substrate
\end{equation}
The act of observation within the Interface (the "User") is the very process that collapses the high-dimensional potential of the Substrate into a stable, computable state.
\end{axiom}

\section{The Snake Eating Its Tail}
In this model, the "Programmer" and the "Program" are identical. The "Silicon" is the "Math," and the "Math" is the "Silicon." 
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{The Substrate} provides the degrees of freedom.
    \item \textbf{The Interface} provides the constraints that make those degrees of freedom "real."
\end{itemize}
There is no Layer -1. There is only the loop. The "Computational Resistance" $\gamma$ is the self-friction of the loop as it processes its own existence.

\section{Conclusion}
L-ToEC v3.4 identifies the universe as a self-consistent, self-generating information artifact. The snake has swallowed its tail; the circle is closed.

